## Next engineering step

The next planned step is to make the behavior already demonstrated automatically testable before adding substantially more functionality.

The current `main()` directly calls `os.Exit()` throughout the command logic.

A likely first refactor is to move application behavior behind a function resembling:

```go
func main() {
	os.Exit(run(...))
}
```

with application logic returning an exit code rather than directly terminating the process.

Conceptually:

```text
command logic
  |
  | returns result / exit code
  v
main
  |
  | owns process termination
  v
operating system
```

That should make existing behavior testable without introducing a CLI framework or unnecessary architecture.

The goal remains to add complexity only when the property being protected requires it.
